Z||000000||jhar1987||10-31-1999||06:56 PM||||does a code 42 on a dis motor mean the module under the coil packs is bad??||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-31-1999||07:15 PM||||I've gotten that one only once. It was when I started the car and my hand slipped off the key.<P>If the car is running OK, try checking all the electrical connectors. If anything is loose it might cause this. Check all the fragging grounds, there's nearly a dozen of them all over the block.<P>That I can tell, other than stupid things like above, only the ECM or the brick could cause this. As far as I can tell DIS motors don't use Tach Filters, at least not as a seperate part. The "brick" consists of the 2 coils, the ingition controller, and the crank pickup.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jhar1987||10-31-1999||07:22 PM||||theogre thanks for the reply. the car hasn't run good for awhile, i still have idle trouble and have replaced everything but the ecm. i do have another "brick" that i could try.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||10-31-1999||08:06 PM||||Don't call him "theorge" he gets very upset and trashes his cage. Just call him "orge" and everything will be OK....I just hope it ain't too late.||||reg||11
Z||000004||theogre||10-31-1999||08:22 PM||||is yours an automatic?<P>You might have a bad gasket under the TBI. especially in an automatic car. The gasket tends to block the IAC passage when it gets old. In automatics the air cleaner has a nasty habbit of hitting the trunk wall. this messes up the TBI base gasket.<P>check all the vac lines, and espacially the PCV valve line. clamp the PCV line to the manifold. Don't over tighten the clamp.||||reg||1
